<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — StockAlert by Loomic"
  appName="StockAlert"
  lastUpdated="February 15, 2026"
>
  <p>This Privacy Policy describes how Loomic ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and shares information when you install and use the StockAlert application ("the App") through the Shopify platform.</p>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <p><strong>In short:</strong> StockAlert captures customer interest when products are out of stock and notifies them when items are back. We only access the data necessary to provide this service, and we never sell your data to third parties.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>When you install and use StockAlert, we access certain information from your Shopify store through Shopify's APIs and collect information from customers who sign up for notifications. Specifically:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Product data:</strong> Product titles, IDs, variant information, and inventory levels. We use this to track which products are out of stock and when they're restocked.</li>
    <li><strong>Customer signup data:</strong> Email addresses of customers who request to be notified when a product is back in stock. This is collected directly from customers via the notification signup form.</li>
    <li><strong>Store information:</strong> Your store domain and basic store settings needed to operate the App.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Customer email addresses are collected with explicit consent when they choose to sign up for restock notifications on your storefront.</p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <p>We use the information we collect solely to provide and improve the StockAlert service:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>To display a "Notify Me" form on out-of-stock products</li>
    <li>To store customer email addresses for restock notifications</li>
    <li>To send automated emails when products are back in stock</li>
    <li>To display demand analytics in the App dashboard</li>
    <li>To track notification-to-purchase conversion rates</li>
    <li>To improve the effectiveness of restock notifications</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Data Storage and Security</h2>
  <p>We store customer email addresses and notification preferences on secure servers. We implement industry-standard security measures to protect your data, including encrypted connections (TLS/SSL) for all data in transit and secure hosting infrastructure.</p>
  <p>Email addresses are stored securely and only used for the purpose of sending restock notifications.</p>

  <h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your data or your customers' data to any third parties. We may share data only in these limited circumstances:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email delivery services:</strong> We use email service providers to send restock notifications. These providers process data on our behalf under strict contractual obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Infrastructure providers:</strong> We use hosting services to run the App. These providers process data on our behalf under strict contractual obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal requirements:</strong> We may disclose information if required by law or in response to valid legal processes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>We retain notification signup data for as long as you have the App installed or until the customer unsubscribes. When you uninstall StockAlert, we delete all data associated with your store within 30 days of receiving Shopify's uninstall webhook. This includes all customer email addresses and notification preferences.</p>

  <h2>6. Your Rights and Your Customers' Rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on location, you and your customers may have certain rights regarding personal data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access:</strong> You or your customers can request a copy of stored data.</li>
    <li><strong>Correction:</strong> You or your customers can request that we correct any inaccurate data.</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> Customers can unsubscribe from notifications at any time. You can request deletion of all data by uninstalling the App or contacting us directly.</li>
    <li><strong>Data portability:</strong> You can export notification signup data from within the App.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We respond to data subject requests within 30 days. We also comply with Shopify's mandatory privacy webhooks (customer data requests, customer data erasure, and shop data erasure) to ensure your customers' rights are respected.</p>

  <h2>7. GDPR Compliance</h2>
  <p>For users in the European Economic Area (EEA), United Kingdom, or Switzerland: we process personal data as a data processor on behalf of you, the merchant (data controller). Customer consent for email notifications serves as the legal basis for processing their email addresses. We do not transfer data outside the EEA unless adequate protections are in place.</p>

  <h2>8. CCPA / US Privacy Laws</h2>
  <p>For California residents and residents of other US states with privacy legislation: we do not sell personal information. We do not use personal information for purposes other than providing the StockAlert service as described in this policy. You or your customers may contact us to exercise rights under applicable state privacy laws.</p>

  <h2>9. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
  <p>StockAlert may use minimal cookies or local storage on your storefront solely to enhance the notification signup experience (e.g., remembering if a customer already signed up). We do not use cookies for advertising or cross-site tracking purposes.</p>

  <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>StockAlert is a business-to-business application designed for Shopify merchants. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 16. If a minor signs up for notifications, it is the merchant's responsibility to ensure compliance with applicable laws.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make changes, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. We encourage you to review this policy periodically. Continued use of the App after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, your data, or wish to exercise your privacy rights, please contact us:</p>
</LegalLayout>
